A model plan that fails validation must not reach a capability executor.

A failed operation must not be reported as successful.

A claim that an operation was completed must correspond to a genuine observed execution.

Memory must remain bounded and relevant. The system should not send all historical records to the LLM on every turn, expose another user's session, or treat an old result as fresh evidence.

